  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nEnshrined in Stone: 1st Battalion The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry in the Second World War Vol. 1 + 2\n£35.00\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\nPreviously published in two separate volumes in 1994, this new imprint combines both volumes covering the story of the 1st Battalion (43rd) Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry through the run up to the Normandy landings of June 1944 and its aftermath, the prolonged campaign in Northern France and North West Europe 1944-1945.\n\nThis new edition also includes further photgraphs and narrative to cover the expoloits of the regiment throughout the Second World War and early post-war period as an Allied occupation force in Germany.\n\nIncludes the 43rd Light Infantry Roll of Honour Commemorating the names of those who gave their lives in the Second World War  with deatils of their resting place.\n\nCompiled and edited by John H. Roberts.\n\nPaperback, ring bound, 440 pages.\n\nRelated products\nBugle & Sabre VI\n£5.00 Read more\nRedcoats to Riflemen: A Short History of the Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire County Regiment\n£4.50 Add to cart\nWinston Churchill: Oxfordshire Hussar – A Bugle & Sabre Special\n£2.00 Add to cart\nThe Royal Green Jackets Chronicle 1970\n£3.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
